  "description": "The person model, identified by\u202fhttps://example.com/person.schema.json and based on the JSON\u2011Schema draft\u201104 located at\u202fhttp://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#, is titled **Person** and described as \u201cA JSON schema describing a person object.\u201d\u202fIt is defined as an **object** with a custom format. By default a new person record should contain the name \u201cJohn\u202fDoe\u201d, age\u202f30, and the email address\u202fjohn.doe@example.com. All numeric values must be multiples of\u202f0.5, must be greater than\u202f10 (exclusive) and less than\u202f200 (exclusive). Strings are limited to a maximum length of\u202f255 characters, a minimum of\u202f1 character, and must match the regular expression\u202f`^[A-Za-z0-9_\\-]+$`. No additional items are allowed in arrays, and the sole permitted array element type is string. Arrays may contain at most\u202f5 items, at least\u202f1 item, and each entry must be unique.\n\nA person object must include at least the properties **name** and **email**; other properties are optional but the total number of properties cannot exceed\u202f10 nor fall below\u202f2, and no undeclared properties are permitted. The **name** field is a string between\u202f1\u202fand\u202f100\u202fcharacters. The **age** field, if present, is an integer between\u202f0\u202fand\u202f120 and must be a whole number. The **email** field must be a valid email address. An optional **address** property references the address definition, which itself requires the string fields **street**, **city**, and **zip** (the zip code must follow the pattern `^[0-9]{5}$` and no extra fields are allowed). A **tags** property may be supplied as an array of unique strings, requiring at least one tag. Any property whose name starts with \u201cS_\u201d must also be a string.\n\nThe model restricts values to the enumeration\u202f{\u202fexample,\u202fsample,\u202fdemo\u202f}. It enforces an **allOf** condition that the object must contain a **name**, an **anyOf** alternative that requires a **nickname** string, and a **oneOf** alternative that requires a **gender** whose value is one of\u202fmale,\u202ffemale,\u202for\u202fother. Conversely, the **not** clause disallows any object that includes an **age** property. Finally, the **age** property depends on the presence of **name**, and the **address** property brings its own required fields (street, city, zip).",
  "reference_json": {
    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#",
    "id": "https://example.com/person.schema.json",
    "title": "Person",
    "description": "A JSON schema describing a person object.",
    "type": "object",
    "format": "custom",
    "default": {
      "name": "John Doe",
      "age": 30,
      "email": "john.doe@example.com"
    },
    "multipleOf": 0.5,
    "minimum": 10,
    "exclusiveMinimum": true,
    "maximum": 200,
    "exclusiveMaximum": true,
    "maxLength": 255,
    "minLength": 1,
    "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_\\-]+$",
    "additionalItems": false,
    "items": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "maxItems": 5,
    "minItems": 1,
    "uniqueItems": true,
    "maxProperties": 10,
    "minProperties": 2,
    "required": [
      "name",
      "email"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "name": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 100
      },
      "age": {
        "type": "integer",
        "minimum": 0,
        "maximum": 120,
        "multipleOf": 1
      },
      "email": {
        "type": "string",
        "format": "email"
      },
      "address": {
        "$ref": "#/definitions/address"
      },
      "tags": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "minItems": 1,
        "uniqueItems": true
      }
    },
    "patternProperties": {
      "^S_": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "dependencies": {
      "age": [
        "name"
      ],
      "address": {
        "required": [
          "street",
          "city",
          "zip"
        ]
      }
    },
    "enum": [
      "example",
      "sample",
      "demo"
    ],
    "allOf": [
      {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "name"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "anyOf": [
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "nickname": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "nickname"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "oneOf": [
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "gender": {
            "enum": [
              "male",
              "female",
              "other"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "gender"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "not": {
      "required": [
        "age"
      ]
    },
    "definitions": {
      "address": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "street": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "city": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "zip": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[0-9]{5}$"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "street",
          "city",
          "zip"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  }
